
====================================================================================================
Part 1. Lemma 3 with weights; Theorem 5(d) with the default weights (1/2, 1/4, 1/4)
====================================================================================================

(a) The scan bound '2 n0, surely'. One committed mistake at scan position j_S = n0 (the worst
    case allowed by Lemma 1); H is a list of non-mistakes (it uses its quarter and never hits).
    n0   sched   max queries   mean queries   Pr[queries > 2 n0]   (2 n0)
      8  SUSH           15          13.34             0.0000       (16)
      8  UHSS           16          13.85             0.0000       (16)
      8  rand           36          13.96             0.2914       (16)
      9  SUSH           17          15.09             0.0000       (18)
      9  UHSS           19          16.37             0.7539       (18)
      9  rand           44          15.70             0.2958       (18)
     32  SUSH           63          56.00             0.0000       (64)
     32  UHSS           64          56.46             0.0000       (64)
     32  rand          107          56.37             0.3367       (64)
    128  SUSH          255         225.45             0.0000       (256)
    128  UHSS          256         225.96             0.0000       (256)
    128  rand          323         226.40             0.3651       (256)
    -> S,U,S,H meets 2 n0 surely; the random schedule meets it only in expectation;
       the deterministic order U,H,S,S (same frequencies) gives 2 n0 + 1 when n0 is odd.

(b) The uniform bound 4 n/|M| (= 4 Lambda when |M| = (sigma+1)/(D+1)): mistakes placed at the end of
    the run so that the scan cannot help; H empty. Mean queries against 4 n/|M|.
    n     |M|   sched   mean queries   4n/|M|
     16     1  SUSH          18.94      64.00
     16     1  rand          18.63      64.00
     16     4  SUSH           9.28      16.00
     16     4  rand           9.42      16.00
     64     1  SUSH          75.29     256.00
     64     1  rand          75.56     256.00
     64     4  SUSH          40.09      64.00
     64     4  rand          40.54      64.00
     64    16  SUSH          10.91      16.00
     64    16  rand          11.93      16.00
    256     1  SUSH         302.49    1024.00
    256     1  rand         302.98    1024.00
    256     4  SUSH         164.69     256.00
    256     4  rand         165.68     256.00
    256    64  SUSH          11.01      16.00
    256    64  rand          12.00      16.00
    (With H empty its weight goes to S and U, so U's share rises from 1/4 to 1/3 and the mean is below 4n/|M|.)
    With H a list of non-mistakes, U keeps exactly 1/4:
     16     1  SUSH          24.35      64.00   (scan alone would need 32)
     16     1  rand          24.78      64.00   (scan alone would need 32)
     16     4  SUSH          11.68      16.00   (scan alone would need 26)
